# TODO - Host and asset safety

## Objective

Protect the host from malformed or malicious user-supplied data.

## Acceptance

- Test archive traversal, symlinks, oversized resources and bad saves.
- Use synthetic fixtures and reject execution of imported binaries.
- Constrain mods, network inputs, file access and privilege requirements.

## Evidence

Partial evidence, 2026-11-24: fresh validation passed in run
1795575348175824037-2468367 (70 tests).

`games_assets::archive` rejects synthetic traversal and Windows-drive paths,
link/special archive members, executable extensions and oversize entries.
Portable path checks also reject device aliases, control characters,
ambiguous trailing dots/spaces and overlong paths or components.
Directory members must declare zero payload bytes.

The constant-memory archive budget reserves declared uncompressed bytes and
member counts before processing. Synthetic tests verify aggregate exhaustion,
zero-length members, atomic admission failures, exact-length streamed data,
truncation and persistent rejection after an overrun.

SHA-256 save envelopes detect truncated, oversized, tampered or invalid
versions, using strict caller-provided limits. All truncated save prefixes
are also rejected. Network message budgets are enforced separately by
`games::network`.

The Linux native platform now stages decoded archive members in a private
owner-only directory, using Nix descriptor-relative operations, exclusive
file creation and no-follow opens. An owner-controlled, non-group-writable
parent and trusted ancestors are required. The staging registry rejects
duplicate, case-insensitive and file/directory collisions. Portable ASCII
paths and a depth cap of 64 are enforced; implicit directories also consume
the archive entry budget. An error permanently aborts the transaction;
drop attempts cleanup, and no partial result is returned for conversion.

Seven native synthetic tests exercise private permissions, successful
staging and cleanup, malformed metadata and decoded sizes, exhausted
budgets, existing symlinks and hardlinks, collisions and untrusted parents.
Fresh workspace validation passed in run
1795577220441162807-2787138 (93 tests).

Real archive-format decoding, publication, Android device verification and
mod/process sandboxing remain unverified. The trusted parent assumption does
not protect against another process acting as the same user. Actual host
and game adapters must integrate and test those constraints before task
completion.
